{
  "id": "m3",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "title": "Movie DB watch list",
  "minutes": 30,
  "tagline": "Modelled on a reported Amazon OA: duplicates slip in, removals don't stick, and errors keep running.",
  "tags": ["object identity", "check order", "unsaved writes", "status codes"],
  "lookFor": [
    "`array.includes(obj)` compares by reference. Two objects with the same fields are never equal. Compare ids.",
    "Order of checks: does the list exist → does the movie exist → is it a duplicate → write. Each failure returns immediately.",
    "`.filter()` returns a NEW array. If you don't assign it and save it, nothing changed.",
    "A save that isn't awaited can lose a race with the very next request.",
    "Deleting something that isn't there should say so (404), not report success."
  ],
  "bugs": [
    {
      "symptom": "Adding the same movie twice is allowed",
      "file": "src/services/watchlistService.js",
      "hints": [
        "What does `[{ movieId: 'm1' }].includes({ movieId: 'm1' })` return?"
      ],
      "cause": "`wl.items.includes({ movieId })` builds a brand-new object, which is never the same reference as any stored item, so the duplicate check is always false.",
      "fix": "`if (wl.items.some((i) => i.movieId === movieId)) throw new ConflictError(...)`",
      "pattern": "Reference vs value comparison"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "Second add still succeeds right after the first",
      "file": "src/services/watchlistService.js",
      "hints": [
        "After fixing the duplicate check, the test can still fail. Is the save awaited before the response goes out?"
      ],
      "cause": "`repo.save(wl)` isn't awaited. The 201 goes out before the write lands, so the next request reads the old list and doesn't see the duplicate.",
      "fix": "`await repo.save(wl);`",
      "pattern": "Missing await on write"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "Unknown movie returns 404 but gets added anyway",
      "file": "src/controllers/watchlistController.js",
      "hints": [
        "The 404 is sent. Does the handler stop there?"
      ],
      "cause": "The not-found branch sends a 404 but doesn't `return`, so execution continues: the movie is added and a second response is attempted.",
      "fix": "`return res.status(404).json({ error: 'movie not found' });`",
      "pattern": "Missing return after responding"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "Removed movies come back",
      "file": "src/services/watchlistService.js",
      "hints": [
        "What happens to the return value of `wl.items.filter(...)`?"
      ],
      "cause": "`wl.items.filter(...)` returns a new array that's thrown away. `wl.items` is unchanged, so the save writes the old list back.",
      "fix": "`wl.items = wl.items.filter((i) => i.movieId !== movieId);` then `await repo.save(wl)`",
      "pattern": "Discarded return value"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "(hidden) Removing a movie that isn't in the list returns 204",
      "file": "src/services/watchlistService.js",
      "hints": [
        "How would you know whether the filter actually removed anything?"
      ],
      "cause": "No check that something was removed, so a missing item looks like success.",
      "fix": "Compare lengths before and after; if equal, throw NotFoundError.",
      "pattern": "No-op reported as success"
    }
  ]
}
@@@ ticket.md
# MDB-420: Watch list is unreliable

Each user has one watch list of movies.

## API (header `x-user-id`)
| Method | Path | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/watchlist` | `{ items: [{ movieId, title, addedAt }] }` |
| `POST` | `/watchlist` `{ movieId }` | **201** + the list. Unknown movie → **404** (nothing added). Already in list → **409**. |
| `DELETE` | `/watchlist/:movieId` | **204**. Not in the list → **404**. |

Movies `m1`–`m4` are seeded.
